WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.160
Then Truman announced the official surrender&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:12.400
this is a solemn but glorious hour i wish that&nbsp;
Franklin D Roosevelt had lived to see this day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:21.760
General Eisenhower informs me that the forces of&nbsp;
Germany have surrendered to the United Nations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:31.520
the flags of freedom fly all over Europe for&nbsp;
this victory we join in offering our thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:39.840
to the providence which has guided and sustained&nbsp;
us through the dark days of adversity and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:48.400
into light much remains to be done the&nbsp;
victory one in the West must now be won&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:57.840
in the East the whole world must be cleansed of&nbsp;
the evil from which half the world has been free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:09.120
united the peace-loving nations have demonstrated&nbsp;
in the West that their arms are stronger by far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:18.320
than the might of dictators or the tyranny of&nbsp;
military cliques that once called us soft and weak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.040
the power of our peoples to defend themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:30.400
against all enemies will be proved in the&nbsp;
Pacific war as it was proved in Europe

